/-!
# One global coordinate germ generated by the actual determinant factors

The finite polynomial diagram uses one formal variable and therefore does not
itself provide a common complex point.  The coordinate representation below
does not take zero fibres stagewise.  Instead, every runtime prime supplies:

* its actual factorization occurrence;
* its factor inside the generated relation-action determinant section;
* the prime-dependent normalization of that factor;
* the normalized reciprocal itself, with no separately submitted series.

The unit-history fold consumes those dependent local certificates and
generates one arithmetic-function germ.  Only after that global germ exists
is Mathlib `riemannZeta` installed as its unique analytic realization away
from the pole.  Analytic continuation is therefore a downstream coordinate
uniqueness readout, not an arithmetic producer or rigidity gate.

No complex zero, zero-fibre point, reversal endpoint, fixedness, or critical
line equation occurs in the producer mouth.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxHeartbeats 3000000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

namespace SaturationMonoid
namespace ResponsibilityLifecycle
namespace LivingLawEvolution
namespace ConstructiveRoot
namespace CanonicalUnitArithmeticFactorizationGlobalDeterminantCoordinateRealization

